N2  - AbstractIn strong ground-motion observations, accelerograms are an important material in both seismic research and earthquake engineering. However, the ubiquitous baseline drift in near-field acceleration records has a large impact on the integrated velocity and double-integrated displacement with linear and parabolic drift, respectively. Conventionally, high-pass filtering and two-stage baseline fitting methods are commonly applied in baseline corrections to obtain reliable strong-motion record
